ow: an AP that is not running starts on its backhaul station's channel

opensync-rpi / opensync-lab: the STA channel override freed its object for an AP as soon
as the AP was not running (not started yet, disabled, or being restarted), so it did not
apply then and the AP started on its configured channel. Patch 0008 moves an AP whose CSA
hostapd refuses by restarting its BSS; the restart came back on the configured channel
(osw wrote it into hostapd's config at the re-add: traced on a Raspberry Pi pod, 2026-10-09
10:59-11:01Z), the override asked for the station's channel again, and the AP restarted
about once a minute, off its station's channel and unusable for clients.

Now the object lives as long as the AP's interface exists, and with a station linked on
the radio an AP that is not running takes the station's channel: it starts there, and a
restart lands there. The decision is in ow_sta_channel_override_action.h, free of the
module's state, so that pod/opensync/tests/ow_sta_channel_override_action_test.c tests it
on its own. (The first version of this patch had the decision only: with the object freed
it never applied.) Live: an AP restarted onto its station's channel.

Upstream: an OpenSync core behaviour as released in 6.6.1.0: ow_sta_channel_override_ap_update()
in src/lib/ow/src/ow_sta_channel_override.c frees the AP object when the AP is not running,
and ow_sta_channel_override_ap_get_action() leaves such an AP alone, so an AP (re)started
while its radio's station is on another channel starts away from it. Not reported (the
owner decides).

